<p id="mwDA"><i id="mwDQ"><b id="mwDg">Schistura susannae</b></i> is a species of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Ray-finned_fish" title="Ray-finned fish" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDw">ray-finned fish</a>, a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Nemacheilidae" title="Nemacheilidae" id="mwEA">stone loach</a>, in the genus <i id="mwEQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Schistura" title="Schistura" id="mwEg">Schistura</a></i>. It occurs in small mountain streams which have <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Waterfall" title="Waterfall" id="mwEw">waterfalls</a> and small <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Riffle" title="Riffle" id="mwFA">riffles</a>, where it is usually observed in pools with gravel or sandy bottoms. It has only been found to occur in the Mong Mo river, a small coastal drainage, in central Vietnam.<sup about="#mwt14" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-iucn_status_18_November_2021_1-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"iucn status 18 November 2021"}}'><a href="./Schistura_susannae#cite_note-iucn_status_18_November_2021-1" id="mwFQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFw">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGA">]</span></span></a></sup> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Specific_name_(zoology)" title="Specific name (zoology)" id="mwGQ">specific name</a> honors Susanne Klähr, for the help she gave to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Maurice_Kottelat" title="Maurice Kottelat" id="mwGg">Maurice Kottelat</a> in his field work.<sup about="#mwt17" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ETYFish_3-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ETYFish"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ETYFish-3"}}'><a href="./Schistura_susannae#cite_note-ETYFish-3" id="mwGw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwHA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwHQ">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwHg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

